\f0\b\fs50\fsmilli25333 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 1. Performance Mindset\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs30\fsmilli15200 \cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 Performance is not only about making an application fast. It is about making the user feel that the application is responsive, stable, and efficient on slow devices, weak networks, and real production traffic. A high-performance frontend usually wins on four fronts at the same time:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf5 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Loading:
\f3\b0  how quickly users can see useful content.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Interactivity:
\f3\b0  how quickly users can tap, type, scroll, or navigate without lag.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Rendering smoothness:
\f3\b0  how stable and jank-free the UI feels.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Resource efficiency:
\f3\b0  how little CPU, memory, bandwidth, and battery the app consumes.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf5 \cb8 Rule:
\f3\b0  Performance work should follow the order 
\f2\b measure -> identify bottleneck -> optimize -> verify
\f3\b0 . Never optimize blindly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

